    "94f36d90e5f2b7ff7007683f": "Place the SureFire magazine in Customs storage building 11",

    "684edc10a8af5086d3e6557b name": "Pressure Relief",
    "684edc10a8af5086d3e6557b description": "Light creates hesitation.\n\nDark removes it.\n\nFactory at night doesn’t give you space to think. No distance. No visibility. Just sound, timing, and decisions you don’t get to take back.\n\nThat’s where control shows.\n\nGo there when visibility is gone.\n\nOperate without it.",
    "684edc10a8af5086d3e6557b startedMessageText": "Night. Factory. No hesitation.",
    "684edc10a8af5086d3e6557b successMessageText": "Good. You don’t need visibility to stay in control.",
    "684edc10a8af5086d3e6557b completePlayerMessage": "Targets eliminated. No loss of control.",
    "684edc10a8af5086d3e6557b declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "684edc10a8af5086d3e6557b failMessageText": "",
    "684edc10a8af5086d3e6557b note": "Eliminate PMCs on Factory during night raids.",

    "8dab0b7bbea3c6716f43fdb6": "Eliminate 10 PMCs on Factory during night raids",

    // ACT 2 Observation

    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a001001 name": "Surface Contracts",
    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a001001 description": "Skier doesn’t hide his movement.\n\nHe lets you see just enough of it.\n\nSmall trades. Electronics. Things that look ordinary if you don’t know what you’re looking at.\n\nI do.\n\nThere’s a structure underneath it. A route he thinks blends into everything else.\n\nYou’re going to find something tied to that structure.\n\nNot the product.\n\nThe pattern.",
    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a001001 startedMessageText": "Don’t interfere. Just see it clearly.",
    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a001001 successMessageText": "There it is. Exactly where it should be.",
    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a001001 completePlayerMessage": "Recovered what you asked for. Clean.",
    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a001001 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a001001 failMessageText": "",
    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a001001 note": "Recover intelligence tied to Skier’s trade movement.",

    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a101001": "Recover Skier’s routing records from the train depot office near warehouse 3 on Customs",
    "69ea1001b4c7a13f5a101002": "Transfer the recovered routing data",

    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a001002 name": "Supply Discipline",
    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a001002 description": "Prapor doesn’t adapt.\n\nHe repeats.\n\nSame routes. Same timing. Same assumptions.\n\nThat’s why his system holds together.\n\nIt’s also why it’s easy to read once you stop looking at the noise.\n\nBring me something that shows how his supplies move.\n\nI don’t need to touch it yet.\n\nI just need to understand it.",
    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a001002 startedMessageText": "Find the repetition.",
    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a001002 successMessageText": "Predictable. Like I expected.",
    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a001002 completePlayerMessage": "Supply data recovered.",
    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a001002 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a001002 failMessageText": "",
    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a001002 note": "Recover intelligence tied to Prapor’s supply network.",

    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a102001": "Recover Prapor’s supply records from the bunker command room on Reserve",
    "69ea1002b4c7a13f5a102002": "Transfer the recovered supply data",

    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a001003 name": "Soft Channels",
    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a001003 description": "Not every system moves weapons.\n\nSome move need.\n\nTherapist’s network stays quiet because people depend on it.\n\nThat kind of structure doesn’t draw attention.\n\nIt doesn’t have to.\n\nFind me something that shows where her supplies go.\n\nOnce you see the flow… you see the pressure points.",
    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a001003 startedMessageText": "Follow where it matters, not where it’s loud.",
    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a001003 successMessageText": "Good. That’s a stable network.",
    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a001003 completePlayerMessage": "Support routes mapped.",
    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a001003 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a001003 failMessageText": "",
    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a001003 note": "Recover intelligence tied to Therapist’s support network.",

    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a103001": "Recover Therapist’s distribution records from the back office of Pharm 2 on Streets",
    "69ea1003b4c7a13f5a103002": "Transfer the recovered support data",

    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a001004 name": "Closed Circuits",
    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a001004 description": "Mechanic doesn’t deal in quantity.\n\nHe deals in control.\n\nParts move through his system because the right people expect them to.\n\nNo deviation. No excess.\n\nThat kind of structure is tight.\n\nWhich means it leaves very little room to hide.\n\nBring me something that shows how his work moves.\n\nOnce I see that… I don’t need him.",
    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a001004 startedMessageText": "Precision leaves traces. Find them.",
    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a001004 successMessageText": "Good. That’s exactly as controlled as I thought.",
    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a001004 completePlayerMessage": "Recovered his routing logic.",
    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a001004 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a001004 failMessageText": "",
    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a001004 note": "Recover intelligence tied to Mechanic’s technical network.",

    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a104001": "Recover Mechanic’s technical records from the lower Factory office desk",
    "69ea1004b4c7a13f5a104002": "Transfer the recovered technical data",

    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a001005 name": "Clean Channels",
    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a001005 description": "Peacekeeper’s supplies come from outside.\n\nThat makes people assume they’re clean.\n\nControlled entry. Controlled movement.\n\nNo one questions where it starts.\n\nThat’s the mistake.\n\nFind me something tied to how his goods enter circulation.\n\nOnce I see the entry point… the rest of the route follows.",
    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a001005 startedMessageText": "Find where it begins.",
    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a001005 successMessageText": "Clean. Predictable. Exactly what I needed.",
    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a001005 completePlayerMessage": "Import data secured.",
    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a001005 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a001005 failMessageText": "",
    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a001005 note": "Recover intelligence tied to Peacekeeper’s import channels.",

    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a105001": "Recover Peacekeeper’s import records from the first floor of the Shoreline pier",
    "69ea1005b4c7a13f5a105002": "Transfer the recovered import data",

    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a001006 name": "Worn Paths",
    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a001006 description": "Ragman moves what everyone ignores.\n\nClothing. Fabric. Civilian gear.\n\nLow value. High volume.\n\nThat kind of movement spreads everywhere.\n\nAnd anything that spreads that wide becomes invisible.\n\nFind me something that shows how his goods move through the city.\n\nYou control that… you control more than he realizes.",
    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a001006 startedMessageText": "Follow where it spreads.",
    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a001006 successMessageText": "Wide coverage. Quiet movement.",
    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a001006 completePlayerMessage": "Distribution mapped.",
    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a001006 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a001006 failMessageText": "",
    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a001006 note": "Recover intelligence tied to Ragman’s distribution network.",

    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a106001": "Recover Ragman’s distribution records from the Goshan shipping area on Interchange",
    "69ea1006b4c7a13f5a106002": "Transfer the recovered distribution data",

    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a001007 name": "Unmarked Trails",
    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a001007 description": "Jaeger doesn’t use systems.\n\nNo schedules. No structure. No consistency.\n\nJust movement.\n\nThat makes him harder to track.\n\nNot impossible.\n\nEven unstructured routes leave impact. Supplies move. Paths form. Patterns emerge if you know where to look.\n\nFind me something tied to how he moves equipment through the woods.\n\nIf it exists, I’ll see it.",
    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a001007 startedMessageText": "Unstructured doesn’t mean invisible.",
    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a001007 successMessageText": "There it is. Even he leaves a trace.",
    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a001007 completePlayerMessage": "Recovered what you needed. No contact.",
    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a001007 note": "Recover intelligence tied to Jaeger’s off-grid supply movement.",

    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a107001": "Recover Jaeger’s supply notes from the Woods hunting camp",
    "69ea1007b4c7a13f5a107002": "Transfer the recovered field data",

    // ACT 3 Infiltration

    "68498dcea603d454abc11356 name": "Echo Traps",
    "68498dcea603d454abc11356 description": "Everything in this city is still talking.\n\nMost of it just doesn’t realize it.\n\nSignals don’t disappear. They linger. Infrastructure keeps carrying data long after the people using it are gone.\n\nRight now, I don’t hear enough.\n\nYou’re going to fix that.\n\nPlace the devices at active points. Not random locations. Places where information moves.\n\nOnce they’re live, I don’t need access.\n\nI already have it.",
    "68498dcea603d454abc11356 startedMessageText": "Place the devices. Cleanly. If anyone notices, you failed.",
    "68498dcea603d454abc11356 successMessageText": "Good. I can hear it now.",
    "68498dcea603d454abc11356 completePlayerMessage": "Devices are active. No exposure.",
    "68498dcea603d454abc11356 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "68498dcea603d454abc11356 failMessageText": "",
    "68498dcea603d454abc11356 note": "Embed listening devices into active communication points and extract cleanly.",

    "5eca9553f3a992fe7186ffe8": "Place the first listening device inside the Customs office at Big Red",
    "15981ab8ec8aa954a205a4fc": "Place the second device inside the new gas station office",
    "603e1e94b031722bf688626d": "Place the final device inside the crackhouse office",
    "500ee99122dbc04cf35d873e": "Extract without exposing the placements",

    "69d81cd30ffb6f16a7c38e69 name": "Family Debts",
    "69d81cd30ffb6f16a7c38e69 description": "Before this city fractured, movement didn’t rely on contracts.\n\nIt relied on placement.\n\nItems left in specific locations. Picked up by people who knew where to look.\n\nThat system never disappeared.\n\nIt changed hands.\n\nThere’s a package staged inside the fortress on Customs.\n\nPre-placed. Waiting for collection.\n\nThey expect it to be there.\n\nYou’re going to intercept it before it isn’t.\n\nNo noise. No disruption.\n\nIf the pickup arrives and finds nothing wrong, the system holds.\n\nThat’s what matters.",
    "69d81cd30ffb6f16a7c38e69 startedMessageText": "Clear the area. Then take the package without leaving a trace.",
    "69d81cd30ffb6f16a7c38e69 successMessageText": "Good. No reaction. That means it stayed invisible.",
    "69d81cd30ffb6f16a7c38e69 completePlayerMessage": "Package intercepted. No one noticed.",
    "69d81cd30ffb6f16a7c38e69 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81cd30ffb6f16a7c38e69 failMessageText": "",
    "69d81cd30ffb6f16a7c38e69 note": "Secure the dead-drop site, intercept the case, and bring it back intact.",

    "64bfa8d68cfc2ae1e2da5d42": "Eliminate 10 Scavs on Customs to secure the drop site",
    "c2ed95c197979810dd2af094": "Intercept the staged package from the first floor of the fortress under the beds",
    "e8f66e0884d4751636f4ab6f": "Extract with the intercepted package without drawing attention",

    "69d81ce56cd2ce07a50d79d2 name": "Silent Couriers",
    "69d81ce56cd2ce07a50d79d2 description": "Routes don’t move items.\n\nThey move expectation.\n\nSomething gets placed. Someone comes to collect it. No communication. No deviation.\n\nThat’s how it stays invisible.\n\nI’ve been mapping those placements.\n\nNow we test them.\n\nThere are sealed packages moving through active routes. Pre-staged. Waiting for pickup.\n\nYou’re going to intercept them before that happens.\n\nDon’t replace them. Don’t disturb the area.\n\nTake them cleanly.\n\nIf the system doesn’t react, it means we’re inside it.",
    "69d81ce56cd2ce07a50d79d2 startedMessageText": "Intercept the packages. No noise. No pattern.",
    "69d81ce56cd2ce07a50d79d2 successMessageText": "Good. No reaction. That means they didn’t see it happen.",
    "69d81ce56cd2ce07a50d79d2 completePlayerMessage": "Packages intercepted. No interference.",
    "69d81ce56cd2ce07a50d79d2 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81ce56cd2ce07a50d79d2 failMessageText": "",
    "69d81ce56cd2ce07a50d79d2 note": "Replace active weapon caches along existing routes without detection.",

    "b6930a22afb94f56ab426741": "Intercept the sealed package from the gray building shelf at the new sawmill on Woods",
    "68dc5482cd37d4f04dd75455": "Intercept the sealed package from the second floor room of warehouse 6 overlooking the military checkpoint on Customs",
    "7a458d853e490f3cb3ef42cb": "Intercept the sealed package from the stage at the Interchange Christmas village",
    "6f538c7593e38a7f916e18f0": "Extract without exposing the interceptions",

    // ACT 4 Control

    "69d81cf3caf46e08a1002df2 name": "Old Accounts",
    "69d81cf3caf46e08a1002df2 description": "Records don’t disappear when people do.\n\nThey get written down.\n\nNumbers. Movements. Agreements no one was supposed to see twice.\n\nOne of them kept everything.\n\nNot digital. Paper.\n\nA ledger.\n\nLocked away behind KIBA. Hidden where people assume value is measured in weapons, not information.\n\nYou’re going to take it.\n\nNot damaged. Not partial.\n\nEverything.\n\nOnce I have it, their system stops being theirs.\n\nIt becomes predictable.",
    "69d81cf3caf46e08a1002df2 startedMessageText": "Recover the ledger intact. If it’s damaged, it’s worthless.",
    "69d81cf3caf46e08a1002df2 successMessageText": "Good. This is what they built everything on.",
    "69d81cf3caf46e08a1002df2 completePlayerMessage": "Ledger secured. No damage.",
    "69d81cf3caf46e08a1002df2 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81cf3caf46e08a1002df2 failMessageText": "",
    "69d81cf3caf46e08a1002df2 note": "Recover intact financial records from an active trader network.",

    "80d9fe503cbd9866053f7eb2": "Recover the financial ledger from behind KIBA on Interchange",
    "b961749deb014e3407999cbb": "Transfer the recovered ledger without damage",

    "69d81cfdc17c3b97d031ff08 name": "The Shipment",
    "69d81cfdc17c3b97d031ff08 description": "Cargo doesn’t matter.\n\nControl does.\n\nEvery transfer runs on a record. Timing. Routing. Ownership.\n\nThat record decides where everything goes.\n\nRight now, that control sits on a single drive.\n\nThe shipment itself is just noise.\n\nYou’re going to intercept the manifest during transfer.\n\nLighthouse.\n\nTake the drive without interrupting the movement.\n\nIf the shipment continues like nothing happened, it means we didn’t take the cargo.\n\nWe took control.",
    "69d81cfdc17c3b97d031ff08 startedMessageText": "Take the manifest. Leave the shipment untouched.",
    "69d81cfdc17c3b97d031ff08 successMessageText": "Good. They’re still moving it. They just don’t control it anymore.",
    "69d81cfdc17c3b97d031ff08 completePlayerMessage": "Manifest secured. No disruption to the route.",
    "69d81cfdc17c3b97d031ff08 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81cfdc17c3b97d031ff08 failMessageText": "",
    "69d81cfdc17c3b97d031ff08 note": "Intercept a live transfer and extract with the shipment intact.",

    "7003c9afb0e78a6668ec37e3": "Recover the shipment manifest from the trainyard warehouse behind water treatment on Lighthouse",
    "39e306f06c18c3a46d2036f6": "Secure the manifest without disrupting the transfer",
    "09505e3d24603629cddb37ce": "Extract with the manifest without exposing the interception",

    // ACT 5 Fracture
    // Crossed Wires Good Questlines

    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70e name": "Crossed Wires",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70e description": "You’ve already seen how it works.\n\nRoutes. Timing. Placement.\n\nYou didn’t break the system.\n\nYou replaced it.\n\nNow it needs to hold.\n\nTwo of the nodes we took control of are drifting out of alignment. Not failure. Instability.\n\nThat happens when a system starts carrying weight it wasn’t built to carry.\n\nYou’re going to correct it.\n\nFactory. Reserve.\n\nUse the toolkit. Stabilize both points. Leave no signal that you were ever there.\n\nIf nothing reacts, it means the system held.\n\nAnd if it held, it’s ours.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70e startedMessageText": "Stabilize both nodes. Don’t let the system react.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70e successMessageText": "Good. Both lines held. No deviation.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70e completePlayerMessage": "Both nodes stabilized. No response.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70e declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70e failMessageText": "",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70e note": "Stabilize two compromised network nodes without triggering a response.",

    "603207d9f2bef8d2219dd0ca": "Stabilize the Factory server node using a toolkit",
    "69e35ba684eda35b8d279376": "Stabilize the Reserve server node using a toolkit",
    "57f8473740b35132ec9a0012": "Extract without creating observable changes in the system",

    // Crossed Wires Bad Questlines

    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70f name": "Crossed Wires",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70f description": "Systems don’t drift.\n\nNot mine.\n\nEvery route. Every placement. Every correction.\n\nControlled.\n\nMeasured.\n\nWhen something changes, it leaves a pattern.\n\nI’ve been watching those patterns.\n\nMovement where there shouldn’t be any.\n\nClean extractions where resistance should exist.\n\nInformation arriving before it should.\n\nThat doesn’t come from pressure.\n\nIt comes from access.\n\nYou had access.\n\nSo now we test it.\n\nYou’re going to interfere again.\n\nSmall. Precise.\n\nI want to see what moves when you do.\n\nAfter that, I decide what you are.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70f startedMessageText": "Make the change. Let the system react.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70f successMessageText": "There it is.\n\nNot random. Directed.\n\nRoutes shifted. Timing changed. People reacted.\n\nThat doesn’t happen without intent.\n\nYou didn’t just access the system.\n\nYou altered it.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70f completePlayerMessage": "Interference made. System response confirmed.",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70f declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70f failMessageText": "",
    "69d81d08b08a9cf2a881f70f note": "Introduce a controlled fault into the network and observe the system’s response.",

    "69e35e5e06b9d69fd0ec0ed4": "Corrupt the Factory server node using a toolkit",
    "69e35e6154de368f5a3d5206": "Corrupt the Reserve server node using a toolkit",
    "57f8473740b35132ec9a0013": "Extract after confirming the system reacts to your interference",

    // ACT 6 Endings

    "69d81d10f141ade1c2f23cbd name": "Blood Oath",
    "69d81d10f141ade1c2f23cbd description": "You’ve been inside the system long enough to understand it.\n\nRoutes. Control. What moves, and why.\n\nMost people don’t get that far.\n\nYou did.\n\nThat leaves a problem.\n\nAccess without alignment doesn’t last.\n\nNow you make it clear.\n\nUse what I provide.\n\nAct in my interest.\n\nNot quietly. Not indirectly.\n\nVisible enough that anyone watching understands where you stand.\n\nAfter this, there’s no ambiguity.\n\nYou’re either part of the system.\n\nOr you’re not.",
    "69d81d10f141ade1c2f23cbd startedMessageText": "Use the equipment. Make your position obvious.",
    "69d81d10f141ade1c2f23cbd successMessageText": "Good. No hesitation. That’s alignment.",
    "69d81d10f141ade1c2f23cbd completePlayerMessage": "Targets are down. Position is clear.",
    "69d81d10f141ade1c2f23cbd declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81d10f141ade1c2f23cbd failMessageText": "",
    "69d81d10f141ade1c2f23cbd note": "Use Tony’s equipment to eliminate his enemies.",

    "ed9c12d309e06158faa7f816": "Eliminate PMCs using the provided equipment without hesitation",

    "69d81d2211b64abb3f86ee12 name": "Clean House",
    "69d81d2211b64abb3f86ee12 description": "You’ve made your position clear.\n\nThat has consequences.\n\nSome inside the network don’t adjust when control changes.\n\nThey hesitate. They question. They start making decisions outside the structure.\n\nThat’s how systems fail.\n\nThese aren’t enemies.\n\nThey’re liabilities.\n\nYou’re going to remove them before they become something larger.\n\nCleanly.\n\nNo disruption to the rest of the network.\n\nWhen this is done, nothing changes on the surface.\n\nThat’s how you know it worked.",
    "69d81d2211b64abb3f86ee12 startedMessageText": "Remove the liabilities. Keep the system stable.",
    "69d81d2211b64abb3f86ee12 successMessageText": "Good. No spread. No reaction. That’s control.",
    "69d81d2211b64abb3f86ee12 completePlayerMessage": "Liabilities removed. System remains stable.",
    "69d81d2211b64abb3f86ee12 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81d2211b64abb3f86ee12 failMessageText": "",
    "69d81d2211b64abb3f86ee12 note": "Eliminate compromised operatives and restore internal control.",

    "1e9026da7e4c46af8c992148": "Remove the compromised operatives on Streets without disrupting the system",

    "69d81d2e489341684c932b76 name": "The New Boss",
    "69d81d2e489341684c932b76 description": "Control isn’t taken all at once.\n\nIt’s built. Tested. Proven.\n\nYou’ve done that.\n\nRoutes adjusted. Systems stabilized. Liabilities removed.\n\nThere’s nothing left to evaluate.\n\nNow we consolidate.\n\nThis location is more than territory.\n\nIt’s a control point.\n\nA place where movement is decided, not followed.\n\nYou’re going to secure it.\n\nRemove resistance. Establish presence.\n\nWhen this is done, you’re not operating inside the system anymore.\n\nYou’re part of how it functions.\n\nAfter this, nothing moves here without you.",
    "69d81d2e489341684c932b76 startedMessageText": "Secure the location. Establish control.",
    "69d81d2e489341684c932b76 successMessageText": "Good. Control is established. Permanently.",
    "69d81d2e489341684c932b76 completePlayerMessage": "Location secured. Control is absolute.",
    "69d81d2e489341684c932b76 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81d2e489341684c932b76 failMessageText": "",
    "69d81d2e489341684c932b76 note": "Secure Tony’s position and eliminate the remaining resistance.",

    "fd122acd465f88fd577be25f": "Eliminate all resistance at the control point to establish authority",
    "05ebbaa447ffa8affb05b1f1": "Extract after securing the location and maintaining control",

    "69d81d3d82a2da467ea1fdba name": "Loose Ends",
    "69d81d3d82a2da467ea1fdba description": "There’s pressure building in parts of the network.\n\nNothing visible. Not yet.\n\nSmall inconsistencies. Movement that doesn’t align perfectly.\n\nThat’s how failure starts.\n\nWe correct it early.\n\nThere’s a point in the system that needs to be secured.\n\nYou’re going to access it and make sure nothing leaks out.\n\nQuietly.\n\nNo attention.\n\nIf it holds, the rest of the structure stays intact.",
    "69d81d3d82a2da467ea1fdba startedMessageText": "Secure the point. Don’t let anything spread.",
    "69d81d3d82a2da467ea1fdba successMessageText": "Good. No visible spread. That’s what matters.",
    "69d81d3d82a2da467ea1fdba completePlayerMessage": "Access point modified. Exposure initiated.",
    "69d81d3d82a2da467ea1fdba declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81d3d82a2da467ea1fdba failMessageText": "",
    "69d81d3d82a2da467ea1fdba note": "Plant a tracker on Tony’s operation and extract undetected.",

    "a5ab7af2349a3ed39a36cb66": "Plant a tracker on the network access point without detection",
    "04866af5282f607ef18a9a5c": "Extract after exposing the system to external access",

    "69d81d46670bc1df8b8c3ed1 name": "Collapse the Family",
    "69d81d46670bc1df8b8c3ed1 description": "Something is wrong.\n\nNot visible. Not fully.\n\nBut the system isn’t holding the way it should.\n\nInformation is moving too freely.\n\nThat shouldn’t be possible.\n\nWe contain it now.\n\nRecover what you can. Remove anything that could spread instability.\n\nIf we isolate it early, the structure survives.\n\nIf we don’t, it won’t.",
    "69d81d46670bc1df8b8c3ed1 startedMessageText": "Contain the breach. Don’t let it spread.",
    "69d81d46670bc1df8b8c3ed1 successMessageText": "Good. That should hold it.",
    "69d81d46670bc1df8b8c3ed1 completePlayerMessage": "Critical intel exposed. System instability increasing.",
    "69d81d46670bc1df8b8c3ed1 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81d46670bc1df8b8c3ed1 failMessageText": "",
    "69d81d46670bc1df8b8c3ed1 note": "Expose Tony’s operation and eliminate resistance trying to contain it.",

    "89129bf73f1a1cd7195d810a": "Recover sensitive operational intel tied to the network",
    "5ecb271f100905c558efb754": "Expose the recovered intelligence to external parties",
    "81efd48874515f97e6765765": "Eliminate resistance attempting to contain the spread",

    "69d81d50db716124768a70a0 name": "Fall of the Fixer",
    "69d81d50db716124768a70a0 description": "The system is fractured.\n\nRoutes aren’t holding. Timing is off. People are reacting to things they shouldn’t even see.\n\nThis doesn’t happen without cause.\n\nWe rebuild what we can.\n\nRemove what’s compromised. Reassert control where it still matters.\n\nIf there’s anything left to stabilize, this is where it happens.\n\nIf not…\n\nWe’ll know.",
    "69d81d50db716124768a70a0 startedMessageText": "Remove what’s left of the instability. Reassert control.",
    "69d81d50db716124768a70a0 successMessageText": "...\n\nNo.\n\nThis isn’t instability.\n\nThis is removal.",
    "69d81d50db716124768a70a0 completePlayerMessage": "System collapsed. No control remains.",
    "69d81d50db716124768a70a0 declinePlayerMessage": "",
    "69d81d50db716124768a70a0 failMessageText": "",
    "69d81d50db716124768a70a0 note": "Eliminate the remaining operators tied to Tony’s network.",

    "96ff16c0c85a8fff88512685": "Eliminate the remaining operators tied to the network using NATO weapons",

